{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban streaming services from showing trailers or ads on plans labelled \"ad-free\"",
        "additional_details": "Consumers pay premium subscription fees to avoid video interruptions. However, we feel streaming platforms exploit a regulatory loophole by classifying their own promotional trailers as \"house content\" rather than commercial advertising. This forces paying customers to actively click buttons to skip promotional material just to watch a show. We believe an \"ad-free\" contract should mean zero unprompted marketing. Parliament must protect UK consumers from this unfair service degradation.",
        "background": "Legally prohibit video-on-demand and streaming platforms from forcing users to watch unprompted first-party promotional trailers (\"house ads\"), previews, or sponsorships on subscription tiers that are explicitly marketed to consumers as \"ad-free\".",
